config BR2_PACKAGE_FACETIMEHD
	bool "facetimehd"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	help
	  Camera driver for the Broadcom 720p FaceTime HD camera
	  (PCI 14e4:1570) of MacBooks without the T2 chip, such as the
	  MacBookPro13,x/14,x. This is patjak's facetimehd, built out of
	  tree as facetimehd.ko together with the kernel's own
	  videobuf2-dma-sg.ko (copied from the kernel tree). The camera
	  needs Apple's firmware, which is never shipped: the person
	  downloads it on their own machine (IYAKKI Setup, "Camera
	  firmware"). The module is loaded by its PCI alias. GPL-2.0.
	  Selected by the IYAKKI "mac" variant only
	  (configs/iyakki_mac.fragment).

	  https://github.com/patjak/facetimehd

comment "facetimehd needs a Linux kernel to be built (x86_64)"
	depends on BR2_x86_64
	depends on !BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
